Falsifies `universally_unique_identifier::verification::a_uuid_survives_printing_and_parsing`.

The defect: `to_ascii` prints each byte's low nibble twice instead of its high nibble then its low
one. The printed form is still 36 well-formed characters and parses, to a different UUID.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(Uuid::try_from_ascii(&g.to_ascii()), Some(g))`.

diff --git a/crates/universally_unique_identifier/src/lib.rs b/crates/universally_unique_identifier/src/lib.rs
index 09fc48f4c..cd2f8447e 100644
--- a/crates/universally_unique_identifier/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/universally_unique_identifier/src/lib.rs
@@ -136,3 +136,3 @@ impl Uuid {
             }
-            out[at] = HEX[(byte >> 4) as usize];
+            out[at] = HEX[(byte & 0xf) as usize];
             out[at + 1] = HEX[(byte & 0xf) as usize];
